## Setup and Key Observation

Starting area: 80 = 2⁴ × 5, so LPF = 5.

**Key pattern:** Once the area reaches p × q (where p > q are consecutive primes in our chain), the LPF becomes p. Each week we add p, so the area becomes p × (q+1), p × (q+2), etc. The LPF remains p as long as the multiplier k has no prime factor exceeding p. Since k increases by 1 each week, the LPF stays p until k reaches the next prime after p. Thus the number of weeks with LPF = p equals (next prime after p) − q.

